Research and creative activity solicitations bury critical requirements across dozens of pages, amendments, and cross-referenced documents.
The Smith-Atlas Solicitation Navigator reads the sponsor solicitation your team uploads (e.g., RFP, NOFO, FOA, or BAA, plus any amendments)
and extracts its requirements into a structured, traceable table spanning ten categories and 39 elements, from deadlines and page limits to
eligibility bars, indirect cost rules, and submission portals. 

Every extracted element carries a precise citation, including the source file, printed page, PDF page, and section identifier, so a Principal
Investigator (PI) or pre-award research administrator can navigate straight to the governing text and verify it. When the solicitation is
silent on an element, it says so plainly.

The system instructions are AI tool agnostic, so you can easily implement them into your preferred platform, including:

Gemini (Gems)
Claude (Projects)
ChatGPT (GPTs)
Microsoft Copilot (Agents)
Any in-house AI Assistants or Agents

Getting started requires minimal setup and zero coding experience. Simply copy and paste the comprehensive system instructions into your AI tool,
then upload the accompanying process file to its knowledge area.

What Your Team Gets in Every Extraction:
 
- A comprehensive ten-category, 39-element requirements table.
- Precise citations for every substantive answer, including the source file, printed page, PDF page, and section, to simplify verification.
- Expanded detail on the elements that get proposals rejected, such as deadlines, page and formatting limits, budget ceilings, indirect cost and
redaction rules, required forms, and eligibility restrictions.
- Requirements changed by amendments are traced through the full chain, so your team can see the governing version and historical development.

